From 88c1ad8da4f572b7fcb0fc7ee156d1199539f6d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bearyjd <28201062+bearyjd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:09:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] genesys: GL126, log what the magazine load saw when a
 program op fails

On one unit "Load film" fails after the magazine edge and the 600 ms
settle. LOAD's first motor completion (op 24, mask 0xfb want 0xf0)
reads 0xfc first and last and times out. The log cannot say why. Poll
records are logged only when a program succeeds, and nothing logs the
status word at the edge, the registers checked after the settle, or
what LOAD itself read before op 24.

Log those values at DBG_info, next to the other magazine lines:

- at the edge, the reg 0x101 poll the edge was seen on, in the "edge
  seen" line. Reg 0x01 and regs 0x3b/0x3c are not read at the edge, so
  they are not logged there;
- after the settle, the reg 0x101, reg 0x01 and regs 0x3b/0x3c values
  the post-edge check reads. Until now they appeared only in its
  refusal;
- the reg 0x32 value LOAD's op 0 reads, whether or not the load
  succeeds;
- when a magazine program op fails, the polls of that program before
  it (op, first/last value, poll count, ms; a best-effort poll that ran
  out of time is labelled so), the poll that timed out, and the last
  reg 0x100/0x101 values the program's own Read ops returned. RunResult
  gains timed_out for the poll that timed out, filled at the three
  throw sites.

Every value logged was already being read. No transfer is added,
removed or reordered, and nothing else changes: no timing, budget or
recovery.

To test this offline, the test USB device gets an optional reply hook
for IN control transfers and an ordered transfer log. The test scanner
interface adds its register and buffer methods, which are USB traffic
on hardware, and its sleeps to the log. A poll loop is stored once with
a repeat count. Both are off unless a test turns them on.

A probe (tests/test_sane_magazine.py in the companion driver
repository) drives the ejected Load film flow through OPEN and LOAD:
every poll matching, and reg 0x101 frozen at 0xfc from op 24 and from
op 38. In all three the transfer sequence, sleeps included, is
identical byte for byte to goldens recorded from 18bea9b32 plus only
these test hooks (tests/gen_gl126_load_film_goldens.sh there), and the
two failures show the new lines.
